  <content>
  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="2c4b3d09-ef7f-4dc9-88bc-62b23bd166e1">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para>1. The number of hours worked, \(x\), and the total dollars earned, \(y\), have a strong positive relationship.</para>
      <para>Explain what it means to have a strong positive relationship in this situation.</para>
    </para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para>As the number of hours worked increases, the total dollars earned decreases.</para>
          <para>As the number of hours worked increases, the total dollars earned increases.</para>
          <para>As the number of hours worked decreases, the total dollars earned increases.</para>
          <para>As the number of hours worked increases, the total dollars earned remains unchanged.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>As the number of hours worked increases, the total dollars earned increases.</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is as the number of hours worked increases, the total dollars earned increases. </para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
